<%- include('_partials/nav') %>

<main class="container page-container">
    <section class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Access &amp; Economic Requests</span>
        <h1>Start with a conversation</h1>
        <p class="lead">Web Chat is the active entry point. Kurukoo records a request and presents only the next action supported by the relevant provider, identity, and payment boundary.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="access-grid" aria-label="Current access and economic boundaries">
        <article class="access-card">
            <h2>Free consumer core</h2>
            <p>Consumers can start with Web Chat, requests, reminders and account tools without choosing a paid plan. A request can still require a separate confirmed provider quote or configured payment boundary before it progresses.</p>
            <a href="/chat" class="btn btn-primary">Start in Web Chat</a>
        </article>

        <article class="access-card">
            <h2>Points, not money</h2>
            <p>Points are loyalty and contribution units. They are not cash, stored value, a payout promise or a substitute for a verified payment. Eligible contributor rewards are recorded only after evidence review.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="access-card">
            <h2>Payment &amp; escrow</h2>
            <p>Economic Requests can model a payment and escrow lifecycle, but a payment service provider is not configured for this deployment. No public page should imply that a charge, payout, or escrow release can be completed here.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="access-card">
            <h2>Providers &amp; businesses</h2>
            <p>Provider and business revenue may use approved subscriptions, lead access, platform fees or other published commercial terms. No public plan activates verification, matching, catalogue availability or payment settlement by itself.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="access-card">
            <h2>Sponsored placement</h2>
            <p>Kurukoo-sponsored placement and external advertising inventory are separate concepts. Any paid promotion is labelled, never treated as verified-provider evidence, and remains unavailable unless the advertising authority has active eligible inventory.</p>
        </article>
    </section>

    <section class="access-note">
        <h2>How an eligible request proceeds</h2>
        <p>Describe the need in Web Chat. Kurukoo evaluates the request, preserves the conversation through any required sign-in step, and presents a provider, quote, payment, or fulfilment action only when the necessary integration and data are available.</p>
    </section>
</main>

